  "domain": "artificial-intelligence",
  "definition": "Rectified Flow is a generative modelling framework that trains a velocity field to transport samples along straight-line trajectories in the ODE sense between a source noise distribution and a target data distribution. By reflow iterations\u2014repeatedly pairing coupled samples and re-training\u2014the learned trajectories become increasingly linear, minimising the number of function evaluations (NFEs) required at inference time. The approach unifies flow matching and score-based diffusion models, offering competitive image and video generation quality with substantially faster sampling compared to standard diffusion schedules.",
